.TH INVARIFS 7 "2026-09" "InvariantFS" "Miscellaneous Information"
.SH NAME
invarifs \- InvariantFS volume format, environment and codecpack ABI overview
.SH DESCRIPTION
InvariantFS is a semantic, content-addressed filesystem with a
bit-exactness invariant: every compression is verified by
decompress-and-compare before it is trusted; containers (ZIP/TAR, and
external formats via containerpacks) are decomposed into member inodes
that flow through the whole codec pipeline recursively; transcodes happen
only where bit-exactness is proven per file. The on-disk format is the
InvariFS volume format v2 (magic
.RB \(dq InvariFS\e0 \(dq);
the de-facto spec is
.I invarifs.h
plus
.I volume.c
in the source tree.
.SH VOLUME FORMAT
The inode area is append-only:
.B [INOD rec_len ... CRC][DELT tombstone CRC]
pairs; v2 tombstones kill by record position (the
.I file_size
field), legacy ones by inode id. Per-file metadata lives in an
.B INO2
extension block appended after the AST recipe inside the record: type,
mode, uid/gid, mtime/atime, nlink, symlink target, xattr TLVs. Directory
anchors are records named
.RB \(dq path/ \(dq.
Hard links clone the record under a new name sharing the inode.
.PP
Superblock flags:
.B VOLF_READONLY
(operator/tool hold),
.B VOLF_META2
(records may carry the INO2 ext; old readers skip unknown extensions via
.I rec_len ),
.B VOLF_RO_SPACE
(the free-space latch that raises READONLY when blocks run out).
Endianness: host little-endian (x86_64).
.PP
Data lives in zones: RAW (unprocessed segments), TEXT (cross-file PPMd
batch members, ReiserFS-style packing into 4 MiB batches sorted by
language family), BINARY (binary ZSTD(+BCJ) batches). Every file carries a
storage-class stamp (an internal
.B invfs.class
xattr: UNCOMPRESSIBLE, CODEC, CONTAINER, GENERIC, GENERIC_MEMLIMIT,
GENERIC_GUARD, TEXT, BATCHED_BIN, DEFER_ENOSPC) that records which codec
owns it and arms the retry logic when a newer codecpack generation
appears.
