.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B INVFS_META_FRAC
mkfs: metadata zone divisor (default 64)
.TP
.B INVFS_SWEEP_INTERVAL
invf-fuse: background sweep period in seconds (default: off)
.TP
.B INVFS_PROFILE
codec effort: fast|balanced|dense|archive (default balanced)
.TP
.B INVFS_ARC_BYTES
ARC cache budget (default 256M; see \-o arc_limit)
.TP
.B INVFS_DEC_MEM_LIMIT
decoder working-set limit (default 512M)
.TP
.B INVFS_MIN_GAIN_PCT
UNCOMPRESSIBLE benefit threshold (default 0.5)
.TP
.B INVFS_CODECPACKS
colon-separated extra codecpack search dirs
.TP
.B INVFS_TOOLS
external codec tool search dir (first priority)
.TP
.B INVFS_AUTO_RECOVER
0 disables DIRTY->CLEAN auto-recovery at mount
.TP
.B INVFS_IMPORT_PREFIX
invf-import: import under this directory
.TP
.B INVFS_IMPORT_KEEP_OWNER
invf-import: 1 keeps source uid/gid (default 0)
.TP
.B INVFS_RAW_WATERMARK
invf-fuse: RAW fill % that kicks an early sweep
.TP
.B INVFS_DEV1
second device path of a two-device (WP25) volume
.TP
.B INVFS_DEBUG, INVFS_DEBUG_PACKS
extra engine/pack diagnostics on stderr
.TP
.B INVFS_PACK_SANDBOX
0 disables the Landlock sandbox on pack helpers
.SH CODECPACKS
External codecs and container formats plug in as
.I codecpacks :
directories
.IB name .codecpack
containing a
.B manifest
(key = value) plus helper programs. Search order:
.BR $INVFS_CODECPACKS
(colon-separated), then
.BR /usr/lib/invfs/codecpacks .
Helper binaries named in the manifest resolve through
.BR $INVFS_TOOLS ,
.BR /usr/lib/invfs/tools ,
the pack's own
.B bin/
directory, then PATH. A pack whose tools are missing is skipped: affected
files wait RAW and unstamped until the tool appears.
.PP
Manifest keys:
.BR name ,
.BR algo
(6-bit on-disk id),
.BR type
.RB ( container
or absent for a whole-file codec),
.BR pack_version
(manifest format),
.B generation
(encoder-set version; bumping re-arms GENERIC_GUARD/UNCOMPRESSIBLE
retries),
.BR caps ,
.BR dec_mem ,
.B sniff.magic / sniff.offset / sniff.ext ,
and for codecs
.BR encode / decode
plus optional
.BR estimate ,
or for containers the four commands
.BR enumerate / extract / strip / rebuild
plus optional
.B map
(seekable reads without the pack) and
.BR estimate .
Commands are fixed argv with
.BR {in} , {out} , {idx} , {dir} , {recipe} , {pack}
placeholders; no shell; exit 0 = ok, anything else = refuse. The FS
memcmps a guard rebuild against the original before committing anything;
a lying pack simply loses the file to generic storage.
.PP
The full ABI (v1.1: seekable containers, DEFER_ENOSPC, codec profiles) is
documented in
.I impl_docs/WP16-containerpacks.md
and
.I impl_docs/WP10-textzone-codec-registry.md
in the source tree (packaged as the documentation of the invfs source
package).
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /usr/lib/invfs/codecpacks
System codecpack directory.
.TP
.B /usr/lib/invfs/tools
Shared external codec tool directory.
.TP
.B /etc/invfs/volumes
Volume list read by
.BR invfs-verify.service (8)
(one image/device path per line).
